  "type": "MULTIPLE_CHOICE",
  "data": {
    "body": "Consider the basis $S$ for $\\mathbb{R}^{3}$ given by\n\n\n\\[\nS=\\left\\{\\left[\\begin{array}{l}\n2 \\\\\n1 \\\\\n0\n\\end{array}\\right],\\left[\\begin{array}{l}\n0 \\\\\n1 \\\\\n2\n\\end{array}\\right],\\left[\\begin{array}{l}\n2 \\\\\n0 \\\\\n1\n\\end{array}\\right]\\right\\} .\n\\]\n\nApplying the Gram-Schmidt process to $S$ produces which orthonormal basis for $\\mathbb{R}^{3}$ ?",
    "solution": [
      2
    ],
    "answerChoices": [
      {
        "id": "5dd8c35e-292b-4dfe-a1a8-6713227961c2",
        "index": 0,
        "body": "$\\left\\{\\left[\\begin{array}{l}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{array}\\right], \\frac{1}{5}\\left[\\begin{array}{r}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 10\\end{array}\\right], \\frac{1}{2}\\left[\\begin{array}{r}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{array}\\right]\\right\\}$",
        "questionId": "915677c9-8118-41ea-9bdf-3b7d775127aa",
